    "notes": "Model: owner-FCF DCF, component route (dcf-methods routing: US operating company, specialty contractor). First valuation of this ticker; no memory entry. FY0 is FY2026E, not FY2025: nine months are reported, the year is guided (revenue 41.3-41.6bn, FCF 2.5-3.0bn) and the balance sheet anchor is 30 Sep 2026, so starting the build at FY2025 would count nine months of FY2026 cash twice (once in the flows, once in net debt). Year 1 is FY2027. Q4-2026 cash flow (~0.3-0.8bn, roughly $2-5/share) is left out of both the flows and net debt, which is slightly conservative. reported_fcf and last_fcf are the FY2026 guidance midpoint, not an actual; FY2025 actual reported FCF was 1,620.8 and owner FCF 1,326.6. Interest income is not stripped because the company carries net debt. Growth paths are organic only from the FY2026E base: no further acquisitions are modelled and no acquisition cash is deducted, i.e. future M&A is assumed value-neutral. Acquired-intangible amortisation therefore runs off in da_pct_path (it is non-cash but tax-deductible). Buybacks: none in 9M-2026, 134.6 in FY2025; the flat share count is a modelling convention that Quanta funds mainly through net-share settlement (the award-tax line), not open-market repurchases. Working-capital capture is negative: a contractor's receivables and contract assets grow with revenue. 2026 was the opposite (contract liabilities rose from 3.26bn to 5.54bn and DSO fell from 66 to 50 days), which is why FY2026 guided FCF sits above the component-built year-1 figure; that prepayment inflow is not carried forward.",
